{
 "id": "football-rankings",
 "title": "Football Group Rankings",
 "pattern": "sorting",
 "level": "medium",
 "statement": "<p>A football championship has teams in groups. Every match is between two teams of the same group. Rank the teams in each group.</p><p>A win gives 3 points, a draw 1, a loss 0. Within a group, a team ranks higher if it has, in this order:</p><ol><li>more points;</li><li>if tied, more goals scored in total;</li><li>if still tied, more <b>alternate points</b> (win 5, draw 3, loss 1);</li><li>if still tied, the earlier registration date.</li></ol><p>Write <code>def solution(teams, matches)</code>. <code>teams</code> is a list of <code>[name, registration_date, group]</code>, where the date is <code>\"DD/MM\"</code> (all in one year) and the group is a string. <code>matches</code> is a list of <code>[team_a, team_b, goals_a, goals_b]</code>. Return a dict mapping each group to its team names in rank order, best first. Teams that played no match still appear. The inputs never leave two teams tied on all four rules.</p>",
 "examples": [
  {
   "input": "teams = [[\"firstTeam\", \"17/05\", \"1\"], [\"secondTeam\", \"04/06\", \"1\"], [\"thirdTeam\", \"24/04\", \"1\"]], matches = [[\"firstTeam\", \"secondTeam\", 0, 3], [\"secondTeam\", \"thirdTeam\", 1, 1], [\"thirdTeam\", \"firstTeam\", 2, 0]]",
   "output": "{'1': ['secondTeam', 'thirdTeam', 'firstTeam']}",
   "why": "secondTeam: win + draw = 4 points. thirdTeam: draw + win = 4 points. Tied, so goals: secondTeam scored 4, thirdTeam 3. firstTeam lost twice."
  },
  {
   "input": "teams = [[\"alpha\", \"01/01\", \"A\"], [\"beta\", \"02/01\", \"A\"], [\"gamma\", \"03/01\", \"A\"], [\"delta\", \"04/01\", \"A\"]], matches = [[\"alpha\", \"beta\", 1, 0], [\"alpha\", \"gamma\", 0, 1], [\"alpha\", \"delta\", 0, 1], [\"beta\", \"gamma\", 1, 1], [\"beta\", \"delta\", 1, 1], [\"gamma\", \"delta\", 0, 0]]",
   "output": "{'A': ['gamma', 'delta', 'alpha', 'beta']}",
   "why": "gamma and delta each have 1 win and 2 draws: 5 points, 2 goals, 11 alternate points. Fully tied on results, so the earlier registration (gamma, 03/01) goes first. alpha has 3 points, beta 2."
  },
  {
   "input": "teams = [[\"red\", \"10/03\", \"2\"], [\"blue\", \"11/03\", \"2\"], [\"green\", \"12/03\", \"2\"], [\"gold\", \"13/03\", \"2\"]], matches = [[\"red\", \"green\", 2, 0], [\"gold\", \"red\", 1, 0], [\"green\", \"red\", 1, 0], [\"blue\", \"green\", 1, 1], [\"blue\", \"gold\", 0, 0], [\"gold\", \"blue\", 1, 1]]",
   "output": "{'2': ['gold', 'green', 'blue', 'red']}",
   "why": "gold has 5 points, green 4. red (1 win, 2 losses) and blue (3 draws) both have 3 points and 2 goals. Alternate points break it: red 5 + 1 + 1 = 7, blue 3 + 3 + 3 = 9, so blue is ahead even though red registered earlier."
  }
 ],
